# NUDL 0.3 EBNF Draft

This grammar records the intended language shape. It is not a claim that every production is implemented in the native C++ compiler. Grammar and implementation differences should be covered by shared conformance fixtures.

```ebnf
program          = { declaration } , EOF ;
declaration      = schema_decl | data_decl | function_decl | binding_decl
                 | statement ;

schema_decl      = "schema" , identifier , "{" , { schema_field } , "}" ;
schema_field     = identifier , ":" , type , [ "required" ] , [ "=" , expression ] ;

data_decl        = "data" , identifier , ":" , identifier , "{"
                 , { record } , "}" ;
record           = "{" , [ field_values ] , "}" ;
field_values     = field_value , { "," , field_value } ;
field_value      = identifier , ":" , expression ;

function_decl    = "fn" , identifier , "(" , [ parameters ] , ")"
                 , [ "->" , type ] , block ;
parameters       = parameter , { "," , parameter } ;
parameter        = identifier , ":" , type ;

binding_decl     = ( "let" | "const" ) , identifier , [ ":" , type ]
                 , "=" , expression , [ ";" ] ;
type             = identifier , [ "[" , "]" ] ;

block            = "{" , { statement } , "}" ;
statement        = binding_decl
                 | "return" , [ expression ] , [ ";" ]
                 | if_stmt
                 | while_stmt
                 | expression , [ ";" ] ;
if_stmt          = "if" , "(" , expression , ")" , block
                 , [ "else" , ( block | if_stmt ) ] ;
while_stmt       = "while" , "(" , expression , ")" , block ;

expression       = logical_or ;
logical_or       = logical_and , { "||" , logical_and } ;
logical_and      = equality , { "&&" , equality } ;
equality         = comparison , { ( "==" | "!=" ) , comparison } ;
comparison       = term , { ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" ) , term } ;
term             = factor , { ( "+" | "-" ) , factor } ;
factor           = unary , { ( "*" | "/" | "%" ) , unary } ;
unary            = ( "!" | "-" ) , unary | postfix ;
postfix          = primary , { call_suffix | index_suffix | member_suffix } ;
call_suffix      = "(" , [ arguments ] , ")" ;
index_suffix     = "[" , expression , "]" ;
member_suffix    = "." , identifier ;
arguments        = expression , { "," , expression } ;

primary          = literal
                 | identifier
                 | array_literal
                 | "(" , expression , ")" ;
array_literal    = "[" , [ arguments ] , "]" ;
literal          = string | number | "true" | "false" | "null" ;
identifier       = ( letter | "_" ) , { letter | digit | "_" } ;
```

## Lexical notes

- Whitespace is insignificant between tokens.
- Proposed line comments begin with `#` or `//`.
- Strings use double quotes with escaped delimiters and control characters.
- `EOF` is an end-of-file marker, not source text.
- Numeric exponent syntax, Unicode identifier classes, multiline strings, and exact escape behavior require further normative decisions.

## Known divergence

The native parser currently supports a narrower subset centered on functions, bindings, expressions, arrays, and control flow. It does not yet parse schema/data declarations or member/index expressions. The browser parser has a different feature set. Treat this EBNF as the design target and the implementation-support matrix as the status record.
